Bladerunner runs Incus VM on macOS using the Apple VZ framework.
It provides a full Incus container environment inside the VM.

Getting started:
  br up       Bring a VM up with defaults, then show next steps
  br shell    Open an interactive shell in the VM
  br web      Open the Incus web UI with single sign-on
  br status   Show VM status

Usage:
  br [command]

Lifecycle:
  boot        Slide a disk in and power it on
  eject       Cleanly power off the active VM (and detach its cartridge)
  reconnect   Nudge the guest clock back into sync after a host sleep, without restarting
  reset       Reset VM to baseline state
  restore     Start the VM by restoring a previously saved state
  save        Snapshot the running VM's state to a file
  self-update Update a .dmg-installed Bladerunner.app in place
  start       Start a new VM instance
  stop        Stop the running VM
  up          Bring a VM up (start with defaults, then show next steps)
  upgrade     Upgrade the running server to this binary's version

Access:
  events      Stream Incus events as JSON
  exec        Execute a command inside an Incus instance
  incus       Run incus commands in the VM
  logs        Stream console logs from an Incus instance
  ls          List Incus instances
  shell       Open an interactive shell in the VM
  ssh         Show SSH connection details

Media:
  disk        Author disk manifests (new, bake)
  disks       List the disk shelf (available .disk manifests)
  watch       Notice cartridges being inserted and offer to boot them

UI:
  menubar     Run a macOS menubar app for bladerunner (status, start, stop, web, shell)
  web         Open the Incus web UI with single sign-on

Config & Info:
  config      Get or set configuration values
  help        Help about any command
  instances   List running VM instances
  notice      Print license and third-party notices
  status      Show the status of Bladerunner VM
  user        Manage SSH-key identities recognized by the local OIDC provider

Flags:
  -h, --help              help for br
      --instance string   Which VM instance to act on (default: the single running one; env BLADERUNNER_INSTANCE)
      --json              Output in JSON format (for scripting/agents)
  -v, --version           version for br

Use "br [command] --help" for more information about a command.
